course: dictionary
lesson: 9592
title: Strenuous: hard work and hard effort
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Strenuous is a word for work that takes a lot of effort, energy or strength. Look at the context: «a bit like the Badger who does nothing strenuous in winter». Badgers sleep a lot in winter and live on fat stored up in autumn, so doing nothing strenuous means not doing anything that takes much effort. Strenuous is the opposite of resting.
explain: Test your guess by swapping in an easy meaning. Try "does nothing hard or tiring in winter". It still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Strenuous can also describe effort that is very determined, as in strenuous efforts to save a forest. Here it does not mean the people got tired. The clues are the word efforts and the goal of saving a forest: they tried very hard.
fact: Strenuous is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a strenuous climb, strenuous exercise.
fact: Strenuous means needing a lot of effort, energy or strength.
fact: «Strenuous» can also describe very determined effort, as in «strenuous efforts».
fact: Strenuous exercise makes your heart beat fast and your breathing heavy, so warm up first and drink water.
fact: Doctors may tell someone who is ill to avoid strenuous activity. Reports and exam texts often use strenuous instead of hard or tiring.
exercise: «The Badger who does nothing strenuous in winter» sleeps underground. What does strenuous mean? | Lying still and sleeping all day | Very colourful | Very quiet | *Needing a lot of effort, energy or strength
exercise: Which activity is strenuous? | *Climbing a steep hill with a heavy bag | Sitting and reading a book | Waiting for the bus | Lying on the sofa
exercise: «The council made strenuous efforts to save the park.» What does strenuous suggest here? | Very sleepy | Badly made | Very cheap | *Very determined, trying very hard
test: Why might a doctor tell someone who is ill to avoid strenuous activity? | It makes them grow taller | *It might take too much of their energy and strength | It is too short to count | It is too quiet to help them
test: Which sentence uses strenuous correctly? | *Digging the garden for three hours was strenuous | Her hat was strenuous | The sky was strenuous | The sofa was strenuous
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to strenuous in «a strenuous climb up the mountain»? | Easy | Green | Sleepy | *Tough
